---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Company | BeaconGuard Assurance"
  description="BeaconGuard Assurance builds independent authorization and assurance infrastructure for consequential AI actions in regulated enterprise workflows."
>
  <section>
    <h1>Company</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard Assurance builds independent authorization and assurance infrastructure for consequential AI actions. The product determines whether an exact proposed action is authorized before execution and preserves verifiable evidence of the decision.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why BeaconGuard exists</h2>
    <p>
      AI is moving from generating content to initiating side effects in enterprise systems. Identity, access, delegation, tool permission, and model safety remain necessary controls, but none should make the AI itself the final authority for a consequential business action.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Make consequential machine actions independently authorized, fail-closed, and verifiable before enterprises rely on autonomous execution in high-risk workflows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Initial focus</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard is initially focused on healthcare operations, financial services, and regulated internal automation where AI-assisted actions can affect patients, customers, production systems, or regulated records.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product principle</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>AI proposes. BeaconGuard determines whether the exact action may execute.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      The architecture keeps identity, delegated authority, invocation permission, customer policy authority, action authorization, business execution, and evidence verification distinct.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Learn more</h2>
